    36	  missing or is not a console, or one whose `variables` is absent or not a map
    37	  while the far side holds one.
    38	- **A command runs at most once.** The far side replaces the file before it
    39	  acts on any command in it, and acts on nothing it failed to replace. So the
    40	  commands of one file are not run a second time, even if the far side stops
    41	  part-way through them. This is at most once, not exactly once: a batch can
    42	  be lost (below), and the rest of a batch is lost when the far side stops in
