     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""A window that answers, for testing and for demonstration.
     3	
     4	**This is not the vehicle.** Nothing here models a spacecraft, and no verb here
     5	has a counterpart on any real vessel. It exists so the rest of the world can be
     6	exercised before the real window exists: the harness needs to run a fleet that
     7	believes it is talking to something, batteries need a telemetry-shaped file to
     8	read, and the contract needs an implementation to be checked against.
     9	
    10	It implements the contract in `docs/diode-contract.md` and nothing more:
    11	
    12	* per-agent directories under DIODE_DIR, each with its own console, output,
    13	  state and telemetry;
    14	* destructive atomic intake -- read the console, then rewrite it with
    15	  `commands` emptied and `variables` preserved, via a temporary and a rename;
    16	* one result file per command, refusals included, named by stamp and command;
    17	* a closed vocabulary with gates, published every pass so a caller can discover
    18	  what is open;
    19	* deferral re-dispatched through the gate at delivery rather than captured at
    20	  scheduling time;
    21	* an operator ceiling that a caller's own variables can only lower;
    22	* a telemetry ring, so a caller that was asleep for a while can see whether
    23	  something moved while it was not looking.
    24	
    25	The verbs are deliberately few and dull. A real window's verbs are the vehicle.
    26	"""
