  3585	        """Run every deferral of this window that has come due, and give each its own result.
  3586	
  3587	        A due command is **revalidated** through the whole chain — phase, gate, interlocks,
  3588	        arguments, dwell, conflict — at the moment of effect, which is §9 check 9 and the reason the
  3589	        acceptance-time answer is not reused; its conflict domain is claimed *here*, at settlement,
  3590	        and not at acceptance. It **expires** if it has waited longer than its own
  3591	        `maximum_queue_age_s`, in simulated seconds: `(tick - accepted_tick) * dt`, so the poll
  3592	        interval no longer decides whether a command's intent has gone stale. And it **reports in a
  3593	        file of its own**, because a command that takes longer than one cycle reports when it is done.
  3594	        Each due entry leaves the queue as it is taken, and its verdict goes into `verdicts` (the
  3595	        cycle's list), so an internal fault part-way leaves neither a settled entry queued nor a
  3596	        settlement unrecorded (child 4's review finding 7). The entry is the parsed command (finding 4).
